# armour/woman/plate: steel plate cut to the woman (P2c slice; re-shaded by LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2-25.3, 27.5): the
# man's breastplate a pixel narrower at the waist, shaped by ONE step-1 shading row across the chest (no sculpting); a
# deep shadow side (half the plate step 1), a narrow step-3 lit band at the top-left, ONE lit ridge (the keel facing down,
# the lit edge facing right and left); the shoulder caps under the pauldrons; a fauld lame under the belt. She is the
# ladder's T6 heroine (lt6w) and the style slice's knight, so every base view carries the finish regions (contracts 3b):
# R the gorget's rim and the fauld's hem, P the breastplate's centre, G the chest socket (below the shading row), N the
# breastplate's lower edge, W a 2x2 spot on the shadow side.
# Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) N (T6 runes) only on the breastplate's lower edge: one designed rune band, not specks over the gorget,
# the chest and the tassets (the blind panel: "scattered 1px specks that look like noise").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i3) T5 wears its people's colour: the surcoat in the accent slot (tabardColor), the skirt's
# cross gilt, so T5 reads red-and-gold, the Mythic white-black-and-fire, T6 blue-and-silver (the panel: "T5 and Mythic
# both red and gold, one outline").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) the Mythic body in its own BLACKENED steel (metal slot, kind 11), not linen: the
# owner saw a white slab with no dark values; dark plate, white-hot edges, gold trim and fire carry it.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i2) T5's breast is its METAL again: a cuirass (lit left plane, a step-4 glint, the shadow side)
# under a gilt neckline and chevron, the people's colour kept below the belt, on the cloak and the plume (the panels:
# "the red tabard covers ~60% of the sprite, only helm, pauldrons and legs show the alloy").
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i2) the hero cuts redrawn (src/hero.py: FURNACE's vents glow in the drawing, KNAPPED's big facets,
# the Mythic's one crack).
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i3) FURNACE's slits run flank to flank with pale heat at their centre and a 2 px ember pool at the
# belly; the Mythic's crack is one 2 px dark seam with fire only at its widest (2 x 2 px Glow); the Mythic's belt in its own
# blackened steel (its leather cells as metal: one dark waist band with the gilt buckle, the panel's 'busy waist').
use person
body woman
role armour plate
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2
legend Q linen 0
legend R linen 1
legend S linen 2
legend T linen 3
legend U linen 4
legend J cloak 0
legend D cloak 1
legend H cloak 2
legend I cloak 3
legend X cloak 4
legend k device 1
legend l device 2
legend F device 3
legend ! glow 2
legend % glow 3

